1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,087
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

2
00:00:03,738 --> 00:00:07,198
اَلْحَمْدُ لله وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:00:07,587 --> 00:00:08,342
Chapter 11,

4
00:00:08,834 --> 00:00:10,390
THE INTENTIONS IN JIHAD(جهاد).

5
00:00:11,770 --> 00:00:17,026
The reward for Jihad(جهاد) only occurs when the intentions for fighting are purely for the sake of Allah.

6
00:00:18,121 --> 00:00:21,018
Anas رضي الله عنه narrated the Messenger of Allah said:

7
00:00:21,621 --> 00:00:25,674
When we return from the Battle of Tabook(تبوك), and we were across from Madina,

8
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:34,510
every step you took, and every valley you cross, there are people in Madina, who were with you.

9
00:00:34,871 --> 00:00:36,101
The Companions asked:

10
00:00:36,815 --> 00:00:40,320
How would they share in the rewards, while they were in Madina?

11
00:00:40,963 --> 00:00:45,889
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: They are the ones, who wanted to join you, but were unable to.

12
00:00:46,659 --> 00:00:48,877
This is in Bukhari(بخاريْ), Abu Daud(أبوداؤد) and Ibn-e-Maja(إبن ماجه).

13
00:00:50,603 --> 00:00:54,695
So, if you made the intentions of Jihad(جهاد), and you couldn't go out to get the Ajr(أجْر) of it,

14
00:00:55,164 --> 00:00:59,901
you made the intentions of Shahadah(شَهَادَة) and you didn't get it, you would get these status of Shuhadaa(شُهَدَاء).

15
00:01:00,338 --> 00:01:01,892
Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألأشعري) said:

16
00:01:02,884 --> 00:01:09,781
A Bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah about the man, who fights for booty and the man will fight to be remembered.

17
00:01:10,249 --> 00:01:12,130
So who is in the sake of Allah?

18
00:01:12,218 --> 00:01:13,465
The Messenger of Allah said:

19
00:01:14,067 --> 00:01:21,590
The one, who fights to make the word of Allah far above is the one fighting for the sake of Allah.

20
00:01:22,091 --> 00:01:23,649
And this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(ألمسلم).

21
00:01:24,440 --> 00:01:27,717
Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) narrated that a man came to Muhammadﷺ and said:

22
00:01:28,301 --> 00:01:31,897
A man wants to go for Jihad(جهاد) and he also wants a worldly benefit.

23
00:01:32,436 --> 00:01:34,753
The Messenger of Allah said: There's no reward for him.

24
00:01:35,388 --> 00:01:38,758
When the people heard that it worried them, they told the man go back again.

25
00:01:39,837 --> 00:01:41,696
Maybe he didn't understand him last time,

26
00:01:41,776 --> 00:01:42,940
he went again and asked

27
00:01:42,980 --> 00:01:44,012
the Messenger of Allah said:

28
00:01:44,092 --> 00:01:45,162
There is no reward for him.

29
00:01:45,567 --> 00:01:49,821
They told him to go a third time but the Messenger of Allah said, the same response

30
00:01:49,935 --> 00:01:55,103
and this is Sahih(صحيح) Hadith(حديث) by Abu Daud(أبوداؤد), Ibn Habban(إبن حبان) and Al-Hakim(ألحاكم).

31
00:01:57,771 --> 00:02:10,898
Abu Ya'la(أبويعلى) said, when the Messenger of Allah allowed fighting, I was already an old man incapable of fighting.

32
00:02:11,966 --> 00:02:17,189
I also didn't have a servant to go in my Place so I hired someone to replace me.

33
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:20,611
And as a payback he would get my share of booty.

34
00:02:22,047 --> 00:02:26,439
He said: I don't know how much the share of booty would be?

35
00:02:26,928 --> 00:02:29,779
So why don't you specify a certain amount of money for me.

36
00:02:29,849 --> 00:02:30,928
Just give me Just give me a salary!

37
00:02:31,690 --> 00:02:33,885
I told him: I can give you three dinars,

38
00:02:34,286 --> 00:02:37,171
when it was time to pay him, I told the Messenger of Allah about it,

39
00:02:37,298 --> 00:02:37,802
he said:

40
00:02:38,151 --> 00:02:42,524
I do not see for him any reward in this world or the hereafter for his fighting

41
00:02:42,611 --> 00:02:44,407
except those three dinners, who you promised him.

42
00:02:45,114 --> 00:02:46,344
That's all what he got out of it.

43
00:02:46,828 --> 00:02:50,013
You know you risk your life you go and fight and only gets three Dinars.

44
00:02:51,677 --> 00:02:55,833
Abu Daud(أبوداؤد), Al-Bayhaqi(ألبيهقي), Al Hakim(ألحَاكِم) and Sahaha Haudad(صحا حوداد).

45
00:02:57,063 --> 00:03:01,702
Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) narrated that Amr Bin Aqyiash(عمر بن عقيش) had lent money with interest,

46
00:03:01,835 --> 00:03:04,336
and he didn't want to become a Muslim until he collects it.

47
00:03:04,939 --> 00:03:09,527
You know a lot of people think I'm not we're gonna make At-Toba(التوبة), until I sort this out or

48
00:03:10,042 --> 00:03:13,340
I'm gonna start practicing until I get this out of the way,

49
00:03:13,419 --> 00:03:15,857
so he wanted to get his money first and then become Muslim.

50
00:03:16,665 --> 00:03:19,430
But on the day of the Battle of Uhud(أحَد), he asked: Where are my cousins?

51
00:03:19,510 --> 00:03:20,237
They said: At Uhud(أحَد)!

52
00:03:20,372 --> 00:03:23,255
He said: Where are so and so they replied, at Uhud(أحَد).

53
00:03:23,366 --> 00:03:24,890
He said about someone else

54
00:03:25,548 --> 00:03:27,033
and he was told they are at Uhud(أحَد).

55
00:03:27,588 --> 00:03:29,950
He went ahead and put on his armor and went to Uhud(أحَد).

56
00:03:31,141 --> 00:03:32,808
When the Muslims saw him, they said:

57
00:03:33,426 --> 00:03:34,450
Stay away from us, Amr(عمرو).

58
00:03:34,609 --> 00:03:36,562
He said: I've embraced Islam.

59
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:40,941
He then fought, until he was injured and was carried away to his family.

60
00:03:41,425 --> 00:03:45,828
Saad Ibn Muadh(سعد إبن معاذ), told his sister to go and ask him whether he fought for the protection of his people

61
00:03:46,244 --> 00:03:48,427
or for the sake of Allah and His Messenger.

62
00:03:49,395 --> 00:03:50,474
She asked him and he said:

63
00:03:51,554 --> 00:03:54,493
I fought for the sake of Allah and His messenger.

64
00:03:55,200 --> 00:04:00,216
He died and entered into paradise without praying even one prayer.

65
00:04:00,978 --> 00:04:03,226
Abu Daud(أبوداؤد), Al Hakim(ألحَاكِم), Sahaha Haudad(صحا حوداد).

66
00:04:04,107 --> 00:04:06,884
Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) narrated, I heard Rasool Allah ﷺ say:

67
00:04:07,662 --> 00:04:10,550
The first whom Allah will judge on the day of judgment is Ash-Shaheed(ألشَهِيد).

68
00:04:11,233 --> 00:04:14,123
Allah will show him His blessings on him and would then ask him,

69
00:04:14,186 --> 00:04:16,386
how Did you use these blessings.?

70
00:04:17,321 --> 00:04:19,766
Shaheed(شَهِيد) would say: I fought for You, until I was killed.

71
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:22,224
Allah will say: You are a lying,

72
00:04:22,652 --> 00:04:26,004
you fought in order to be recognized, as a fighter and you go that.

73
00:04:27,033 --> 00:04:29,830
Then Allah order that he be carried to hellfire.

74
00:04:30,354 --> 00:04:32,165
It’s in Muslim(ألمسلم) An-Nasai(ألنَّسائ) And Al Hakim(ألحَاكِم).

75
00:04:32,330 --> 00:04:34,119
Ibn Masood(إبن مسعود) said: When the armies meet,

76
00:04:34,865 --> 00:04:38,206
the angels descend to write down the men according to their state.

77
00:04:39,055 --> 00:04:41,508
They write down that this person is fighting for money.

78
00:04:42,024 --> 00:04:43,573
This person is fighting for power.

79
00:04:44,032 --> 00:04:45,874
This person is fighting for recognition.

80
00:04:46,294 --> 00:04:48,278
And this person is fighting for the sake of Allah.

81
00:04:48,945 --> 00:04:52,385
The ones who fought, for the sake of Allah are the ones who will have paradise.

82
00:04:53,496 --> 00:04:55,480
Tayeb(طيِّب) the different intentions in Jihad(جهاد),

83
00:04:56,107 --> 00:04:57,472
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) mentions a few,

84
00:04:58,115 --> 00:05:02,904
having a pure intention in Jihad(جهاد) is important since Allah doesn't accept the Jihad(جهاد) of a Mujahid(مُجَاهِد)

85
00:05:03,306 --> 00:05:05,179
unless he's fighting with the right intentions,

86
00:05:05,742 --> 00:05:07,250
Mujahideen(مجاهدين) have different intentions.

87
00:05:07,290 --> 00:05:08,663
Number one, the pleasure of Allah,

88
00:05:10,583 --> 00:05:15,337
there are Mujahideen(مجاهدين) who intend with their Jihad(جهاد), the pleasure of Allah.

89
00:05:15,924 --> 00:05:20,327
They do Because they believe Allah deserves to be served through, this ritual.

90
00:05:21,079 --> 00:05:24,595
They do it for no reason other than gaining the approval of Allah.

91
00:05:25,078 --> 00:05:27,896
The ones with such an intention are a few.

92
00:05:29,261 --> 00:05:29,919
Number two,

93
00:05:30,229 --> 00:05:31,173
LOVE OF ISLAM:

94
00:05:32,663 --> 00:05:36,980
Some Mujahideen(مجاهدين) participated in Jihad(جهاد) because of their love and vigilance, care for Islam.

95
00:05:37,338 --> 00:05:41,277
They want Islam to be victorious, and they want disbelief to be defeated.

96
00:05:41,856 --> 00:05:46,663
You have a lot of people who, they care about the Ummah(امة).

97
00:05:48,250 --> 00:05:51,659
And they cry when they see what is happening with the Muslims,

98
00:05:51,948 --> 00:05:54,115
and they love Islam and they want Islam to be victorious.

99
00:05:54,186 --> 00:05:58,335
So when they fight, they're fighting because they want Islam, that's their objective.

100
00:05:58,708 --> 00:06:01,769
You know, I'm fighting because I want Islam to be victorious.

101
00:06:03,912 --> 00:06:08,869
So Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says: There is no doubt over the validity of the aforementioned two intentions,

102
00:06:09,631 --> 00:06:10,330
number one and two,

103
00:06:10,790 --> 00:06:14,998
Evidence that the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) is basing their Jihad(جهاد) on one of the two intentions

104
00:06:15,410 --> 00:06:19,085
is that they wouldn't care about others knowing about their Jihad(جهاد),

105
00:06:19,744 --> 00:06:21,388
and they wouldn't brag about it.

106
00:06:22,783 --> 00:06:26,194
As long as Allah knows about their Jihad(جهاد), that is sufficient for them.

107
00:06:27,170 --> 00:06:29,139
So that's the acid test.

108
00:06:29,670 --> 00:06:32,710
To tell you, if a person has number one and two,

109
00:06:33,655 --> 00:06:36,797
they don't really care if they become famous, or their names are known.

110
00:06:37,505 --> 00:06:40,434
I did this Jihad(جهاد) for the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

111
00:06:40,989 --> 00:06:42,228
It doesn't matter who knows about it.

112
00:06:43,276 --> 00:06:45,188
That's the sign of the good intention.

113
00:06:45,586 --> 00:06:46,475
They don't brag about it.

114
00:06:47,601 --> 00:06:52,577
You know, they don't go spend a season there and then come back

115
00:06:53,562 --> 00:06:56,645
and try to gain approval of the people through it by bragging.

116
00:06:57,431 --> 00:07:02,596
Yeah, because this recognition thing is a serious problem.

117
00:07:02,770 --> 00:07:05,077
It's a human thing you want to be recognized

118
00:07:06,466 --> 00:07:10,975
and that could interfere with the with the sincerity of the Jihad(جهاد).

119
00:07:12,077 --> 00:07:13,966
Especially when it becomes stylish.

120
00:07:15,339 --> 00:07:16,631
Number three seeking paradise,

121
00:07:18,043 --> 00:07:22,327
Some Mujahideen(مجاهدين) do Jihad(جهاد) for the sake of entering paradise and being saved from hellfire.

122
00:07:24,113 --> 00:07:27,097
This is the intention of most of the Mujahideen(مجاهدين).

123
00:07:28,367 --> 00:07:31,717
And in fact, even when it comes to fighting for paradise,

124
00:07:31,797 --> 00:07:35,918
you know some people could even be very specific about what exactly in paradise.

125
00:07:35,998 --> 00:07:37,480
I mean somebody could fight for Hoor-Ul-Ain(حورالعين).

126
00:07:38,584 --> 00:07:44,104
They're in so much in love with that Hooriya(حورية) whom they never met, all of the fighting is for her.

127
00:07:44,819 --> 00:07:47,414
And they're fighting to impress her because they know that she’s watching.

128
00:07:53,021 --> 00:07:57,835
Now some say: That this intention is not sufficient to reach the status of martyrdom

129
00:07:57,891 --> 00:08:03,213
but the correct opinion is that this intention is sufficient in reaching the status of martyrdom

130
00:08:03,605 --> 00:08:08,317
and there is an abundance of evidence from Qur'an, Sunnah(سنة) and the action of the Sahabah(صحابه) to support that.

131
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:13,151
The ones who say that it's not the intention you would find that among some of the early Sufi(صوفي) scholars.

132
00:08:14,572 --> 00:08:19,718
They held the view that, Not just in Shahadah(شَهَادَة) or Jihad(جهاد)

133
00:08:19,798 --> 00:08:26,231
they held the view that whatever you do in Islam, it should be for the pleasure of Allah and not for Jannah(جنة).

134
00:08:27,850 --> 00:08:32,356
And this is a bit of an idealistic view and it's not really supported by Qur'an and Sunnah(سنة)

135
00:08:32,396 --> 00:08:37,092
because we have a lot of Ahadith(احاديث) that show that if a person is doing it for the sake of Jannah(جنة),

136
00:08:37,403 --> 00:08:44,185
it is valid because it is for the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَل.

137
00:08:44,376 --> 00:08:45,939
Because that is a promise of Allah for you,

138
00:08:46,408 --> 00:08:50,061
it's a promise of Allah to Muslim that Allah will give you Jannah(جنة).

139
00:08:51,457 --> 00:08:52,291
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

140
00:08:52,331 --> 00:08:55,610
إِنَّ اللَّهَ اشتَرىٰ مِنَ المُؤمِنينَ أَنفُسَهُم وَأَموالَهُم بِأَنَّ لَهُمُ الجَنَّةَ ۚ

141
00:08:56,481 --> 00:09:01,782
That’s the contract, that's the contract, agreement. Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

142
00:09:02,163 --> 00:09:09,688
إِنَّ اللَّهَ اشتَرىٰ مِنَ المُؤمِنينَ أَنفُسَهُم وَأَموالَهُم

143
00:09:10,061 --> 00:09:15,044
وَأَموالَهُم بِأَنَّ لَهُمُ الجَنَّةَ ۚ

144
00:09:15,354 --> 00:09:22,418
يُقاتِلونَ في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ فَيَقتُلونَ وَيُقتَلونَ ۖ

145
00:09:22,814 --> 00:09:30,911
وَعدًا عَلَيهِ حَقًّا فِي التَّوراةِ وَالإِنجيلِ وَالقُرآنِ ۚ

146
00:09:31,181 --> 00:09:35,435
وَمَن أَوفىٰ بِعَهدِهِ مِنَ اللَّهِ ۚ

147
00:09:35,841 --> 00:09:41,258
فَاستَبشِروا بِبَيعِكُمُ الَّذي بايَعتُم بِهِ ۚ

148
00:09:41,587 --> 00:09:45,905
وَذٰلِكَ هُوَ الفَوزُ العَظيمُ۞

149
00:09:46,352 --> 00:09:49,441
Indeed Allah has purchased from the believers, their lives

150
00:09:49,568 --> 00:09:52,362
and their properties in exchange for that they will have paradise.

151
00:09:52,975 --> 00:09:58,308
So, it's absolutely fine for you to fight according to the terms of the agreements between you and Allah.

152
00:09:58,864 --> 00:10:02,197
Allah makes a deal with you give me a your sole and your wealth

153
00:10:02,498 --> 00:10:04,070
and I'm going to give you an Jannah(جنة) in exchange.

154
00:10:04,483 --> 00:10:05,349
There's nothing wrong with it.

155
00:10:06,110 --> 00:10:09,608
And if all what you're interested in Jannah(جنة) is the Hoor(حور), that's fine, you can fight for the Hoor(حور),

156
00:10:09,941 --> 00:10:12,714
or the palace or the trees or the rivers, whatever.

157
00:10:13,227 --> 00:10:25,152
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا هَل أَدُلُّكُم عَلىٰ تِجارَةٍ تُنجيكُم مِن عَذابٍ أَليمٍ۞

158
00:10:25,866 --> 00:10:35,591
تُؤمِنونَ بِاللَّهِ وَرَسولِهِ وَتُجاهِدونَ في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ بِأَموالِكُم وَأَنفُسِكُم ۚ

159
00:10:36,448 --> 00:10:42,245
ذٰلِكُم خَيرٌ لَكُم إِن كُنتُم تَعلَمونَ۞

160
00:10:42,829 --> 00:10:51,945
يَغفِر لَكُم ذُنوبَكُم وَيُدخِلكُم جَنّاتٍ تَجري مِن تَحتِهَا الأَنهارُ

161
00:10:52,584 --> 00:10:57,503
وَمَساكِنَ طَيِّبَةً في جَنّاتِ عَدنٍ ۚ

162
00:10:57,884 --> 00:11:01,291
ذٰلِكَ الفَوزُ العَظيمُ۞

163
00:11:02,312 --> 00:11:06,488
O you believed Shall I guide you to a transaction that will save you from a painful punishment.

164
00:11:06,630 --> 00:11:09,122
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا هَل أَدُلُّكُم عَلىٰ تِجارَةٍ تُنجيكُم مِن عَذابٍ أَليمٍ۞

165
00:11:09,988 --> 00:11:14,122
تُؤمِنونَ بِاللَّهِ وَرَسولِهِ وَتُجاهِدونَ في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ بِأَموالِكُم وَأَنفُسِكُم ۚ

166
00:11:14,503 --> 00:11:16,500
ذٰلِكُم خَيرٌ لَكُم إِن كُنتُم تَعلَمونَ۞

167
00:11:16,787 --> 00:11:17,994
يَغفِر لَكُم ذُنوبَكُم

168
00:11:18,990 --> 00:11:24,360
وَيُدخِلكُم جَنّاتٍ تَجري مِن تَحتِهَا الأَنهارُ وَمَساكِنَ طَيِّبَةً في جَنّاتِ عَدنٍ ۚ

169
00:11:24,574 --> 00:11:25,971
ذٰلِكَ الفَوزُ العَظيمُ۞

170
00:11:26,487 --> 00:11:28,043
These are the Ayaat(آيات) in Surah As-Saff(سورة الصف).

171
00:11:28,908 --> 00:11:33,174
You believe in Allah and His messenger and striving the cause of Allah with your wealth and your lives

172
00:11:33,567 --> 00:11:35,416
that is best for you if you should know,

173
00:11:35,908 --> 00:11:40,183
he will forgive for your sins and admit you to garden beneath which rivers flow

174
00:11:40,651 --> 00:11:43,662
and pleasant dwellings in gardens of perpetual residence.

175
00:11:43,984 --> 00:11:45,243
That is the great attainment.

176
00:11:48,183 --> 00:11:49,347
The Messenger of Allah said:

177
00:11:49,736 --> 00:11:53,972
Whoever fights in the path of Allah the time it takes to milk a camel is granted paradise.

178
00:11:54,490 --> 00:11:57,474
Ibn Habban(إبن حبَّان), An-Nasae(ألنسائ) ,At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ), Ahmad(ألحمد), Ibn e Majah(إبن ماجه).

179
00:11:58,220 --> 00:12:02,632
The Messenger of Allah said: Don't you love that Allah forgives you and admits you into paradise.

180
00:12:02,983 --> 00:12:04,274
Then fight the path of Allah.

181
00:12:04,697 --> 00:12:05,864
Rawah Ahmad(رواة أحمد), At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ).

182
00:12:06,611 --> 00:12:08,818
So, now Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) is mentioning all of these evidence,

183
00:12:09,198 --> 00:12:11,214
piece of evidence that it's alright to fight for Jannah(جنة).

184
00:12:12,902 --> 00:12:17,813
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) narrated that on the day of the Battle of Badr(بدر), the Messenger of Allah said,

185
00:12:18,354 --> 00:12:23,784
stand up and face paradise, the width of which is like the Heavens and Earth.

186
00:12:25,346 --> 00:12:28,277
So here Rasool Ullah is telling them fight with intentions of Jannah(جنة).

187
00:12:28,706 --> 00:12:30,515
Stand up and go to Jannah!.

188
00:12:31,364 --> 00:12:33,636
Umair Bin Al-Hamam(عمير بن ألحمام) said:

189
00:12:34,121 --> 00:12:38,291
O Messenger of Allah paradise the width of which is like the heavens and Earth.

190
00:12:38,772 --> 00:12:40,429
The Messenger of Allah said: Yes!

191
00:12:40,843 --> 00:12:42,906
Umair(عمير) was eating from some dates in his hand.

192
00:12:42,994 --> 00:12:48,279
He said: If I'm going to live as long as it takes to finish eating these dates, that's a long time

193
00:12:49,271 --> 00:12:52,034
and he threw them away and he rushed to the battlefield and he was killed

194
00:12:53,708 --> 00:12:55,232
and that's in Muslim(ألمسلم) and Al Hakim(ألحَاكِم).

195
00:12:55,812 --> 00:12:59,476
It appears from the Hadith(حديث) that Umair(عمير) fought for the sake of paradise.

196
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:06,771
Shaddad Bin Al-Had(شدَّاد بن ألحاد) said that a Bedouin came to Messenger of Allah,

197
00:13:07,247 --> 00:13:08,719
he believed in him, followed him.

198
00:13:09,144 --> 00:13:13,379
During the Battle of the Trench, the Messenger of Allah was dividing the booties of war between the companions.

199
00:13:13,807 --> 00:13:14,927
So he gave him, his portion.

200
00:13:14,967 --> 00:13:16,143
The Bedouin said: What is this?

201
00:13:16,863 --> 00:13:18,279
They said: Rasool Ullah sent it to you.

202
00:13:18,914 --> 00:13:21,073
So he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said: What is this?

203
00:13:22,224 --> 00:13:24,558
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: This is your share of the booty.

204
00:13:24,755 --> 00:13:27,955
He said that's not why I followed you?

205
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:31,078
I followed you, in order that I  be shot right here.

206
00:13:31,861 --> 00:13:32,909
And he pointed to his throat,

207
00:13:33,432 --> 00:13:36,075
with an arrow so I can die and enter into paradise.

208
00:13:36,877 --> 00:13:40,468
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: If you are truthful with Allah, Allah will be truthful with you.

209
00:13:41,829 --> 00:13:43,306
And then later, they went to fight,

210
00:13:43,803 --> 00:13:47,491
The Bedouin was carried back to the messenger of Allah with an arrow injury in his throat.

211
00:13:48,499 --> 00:13:51,285
Rasool Allah ﷺ asked if it was him? They said: Yes!

212
00:13:51,491 --> 00:13:55,841
He said: He was truthful with Allah and Allah was truthful with him.

213
00:13:56,412 --> 00:13:57,540
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

214
00:13:58,071 --> 00:14:03,801
O Allah, this servant of yours made Hijrah(هجرة) for Your sake, and then died as a martyr.

215
00:14:04,174 --> 00:14:05,590
I'm a witness over that.

216
00:14:06,780 --> 00:14:07,981
Abdur-Razzaq(عبدالرزاق) and An-Nasai(ألنَّسائ).

217
00:14:08,074 --> 00:14:10,100
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), Rasool  Ullah is witnessing for him.

218
00:14:11,328 --> 00:14:13,131
Notice here how the Messenger of Allah said:

219
00:14:13,623 --> 00:14:14,853
I'm a witness over that.

220
00:14:14,964 --> 00:14:17,616
When all what the Bedouin want was paradise.

221
00:14:18,250 --> 00:14:23,377
If this was an invalid intention, he would have corrected them on the spot when he heard it from him.

222
00:14:24,570 --> 00:14:25,578
So that should be clear.

223
00:14:26,967 --> 00:14:28,374
Number four, SELF DEFENSE.

224
00:14:29,049 --> 00:14:33,457
Some people only fight, when fought.

225
00:14:34,073 --> 00:14:36,089
They have no intension but defending themselves.

226
00:14:36,882 --> 00:14:40,779
Person with such intention is close to the above three mentioned intentions.

227
00:14:41,223 --> 00:14:44,128
But is nevertheless lower than them, in status.

228
00:14:44,668 --> 00:14:48,557
So it's a valid intentions but it's a bit lower in reward.

229
00:14:49,437 --> 00:14:52,579
An-Nawwawi(ألنووِي) states that there are three categories of Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء).

230
00:14:53,485 --> 00:14:56,067
Shaheed(شَهِيد) on this world and the hereafter.

231
00:14:56,668 --> 00:14:58,762
This is the one who was killed in the path of Allah.

232
00:14:59,650 --> 00:15:00,246
Number two,

233
00:15:00,690 --> 00:15:04,650
Shaheed(شَهِيد) in the hereafter alone, but not this world.

234
00:15:05,206 --> 00:15:09,244
This applies to the one, who drowns or the ones who dies in a plague.

235
00:15:09,926 --> 00:15:15,554
What this means is that, you apply to them the Ahkam(أحكام) of Shaheed(شَهِيد) in Akhirah(آخرة) not in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

236
00:15:16,061 --> 00:15:17,594
So you pray on them.

237
00:15:18,217 --> 00:15:21,399
You wash them, give them Kafan(كفن).

238
00:15:22,828 --> 00:15:27,713
So in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) you treat them as dying from a natural cause.

239
00:15:29,420 --> 00:15:30,706
But they are Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) in Akhirah(آخرة).

240
00:15:31,150 --> 00:15:34,680
And then there is Shaheed(شَهِيد) in this world only, but not in the hereafter.

241
00:15:35,060 --> 00:15:37,505
This applies to the one who was killed in battle,

242
00:15:37,822 --> 00:15:40,473
but didn't have the right intentions or stole from the booties.

243
00:15:40,862 --> 00:15:44,199
So this person you, you treat him as a Shaheed(شَهِيد), you didn't Wash them,

244
00:15:44,566 --> 00:15:47,897
don't pray Janazah(جنازة) on them but in Akhirah(آخرة) they're not Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء).

245
00:15:50,670 --> 00:15:54,838
NUMBER FIVE: Both Jihad(جهاد) and booties and this is a very important,

246
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:59,848
there are some who go out with the intention of fighting for the sake of Allah

247
00:15:59,951 --> 00:16:02,350
but they also have the intention of winning booties.

248
00:16:04,112 --> 00:16:06,110
The scholars differed over this situation.

249
00:16:06,945 --> 00:16:14,168
Some consider that this to be an invalid intention and there is no reward for such a Jihad(جهاد).

250
00:16:14,855 --> 00:16:18,458
In fact there's a punishment because such a person was fighting for this world,

251
00:16:19,362 --> 00:16:21,909
but other scholars consider this intention to be acceptable.

252
00:16:22,616 --> 00:16:25,315
And this is the opinion of the majority of the Scholars.

253
00:16:26,037 --> 00:16:29,848
This is the correct opinion because it fits into the actions of the Sahabah(صحابه).

254
00:16:30,586 --> 00:16:31,623
Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) states that

255
00:16:31,663 --> 00:16:36,235
the Messenger of Allah, went to intercept the caravan of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) led by Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان).

256
00:16:36,703 --> 00:16:41,697
This is evidence that's fighting for booty is fine because it is Halal(حلال) source of income.

257
00:16:43,077 --> 00:16:45,588
This refutes the opinion adopted by a Imam(اِمَام) Malik(إمام مالك).

258
00:16:46,262 --> 00:16:47,937
That this is a fight for this world,

259
00:16:48,762 --> 00:16:54,886
there are Ahadith(احاديث) that state to whoever fight for the word of Allah to prevail is in the path of Allah,

260
00:16:55,158 --> 00:16:56,785
and not the one who fights for booty.

261
00:16:57,324 --> 00:17:03,800
But the meaning of this Hadith(حديث) is, if someone had the intention of fighting only for booty.

262
00:17:04,435 --> 00:17:06,698
Then that is an invalid intention in Jihad(جهاد).

263
00:17:07,530 --> 00:17:11,881
Another evidence that's such an intention was acceptable is where Allah says:

264
00:17:12,136 --> 00:17:23,984
وَعَدَكُمُ اللَّهُ مَغانِمَ كَثيرَةً تَأخُذونَها فَعَجَّلَ لَكُم هٰذِهِ وَكَفَّ أَيدِيَ النّاسِ عَنكُم

265
00:17:24,718 --> 00:17:36,371
وَكَفَّ أَيدِيَ النّاسِ عَنكُم وَلِتَكونَ آيَةً لِلمُؤمِنينَ وَيَهدِيَكُم صِراطًا مُستَقيمًا۞

266
00:17:36,935 --> 00:17:38,859
وَعَدَكُمُ اللَّهُ مَغانِمَ كَثيرَةً

267
00:17:39,232 --> 00:17:41,796
Allah has promised you much booty that you will take.

268
00:17:42,669 --> 00:17:45,855
In Surat-Ul-Fath(سورة الفتح). Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ promises the Muslims booty.

269
00:17:46,585 --> 00:17:51,285
One cannot imagine that Allah with promise His servants booty, but this allows them to desire it.

270
00:17:53,077 --> 00:17:55,564
The action of Rasool Allah ﷺ is also evidence.

271
00:17:56,151 --> 00:17:59,604
He has sent many raids on the caravan of the non believers.

272
00:18:00,104 --> 00:18:04,386
Some other references to show that such intention is valid.

273
00:18:04,529 --> 00:18:05,814
Abdullah Bin Hudhaifa(عبدالله بن حذيفة) said:

274
00:18:07,481 --> 00:18:12,263
Rasool Allah ﷺ sent us on a raid, to win booty.

275
00:18:12,802 --> 00:18:14,294
This in Abu Daud(أبوداؤد) and Al-Bayhaqi(ألبيهقي).

276
00:18:15,128 --> 00:18:18,831
This is clear, since Messenger of Allah send them specifically to win booties.

277
00:18:19,342 --> 00:18:24,709
Now taking booty, does decrease the reward but it does not invalidate the intention of Jihad(جهاد).

278
00:18:25,853 --> 00:18:28,564
Abdullah Bin Amr Bin Al-Aas(عبدالله بن عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) narrated Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

279
00:18:29,448 --> 00:18:34,624
Any army that wins and takes booty has received two thirds of their reward.

280
00:18:35,208 --> 00:18:38,718
But if they lose and take no booty, they receive the entire reward.

281
00:18:40,067 --> 00:18:43,057
So the Ajr(أجْر) is still there just decreases and this is in Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم).

282
00:18:43,438 --> 00:18:45,216
So I hope that this point is clear.

283
00:18:46,129 --> 00:18:47,388
NUMBER SIX, Booty.

284
00:18:48,237 --> 00:18:53,026
There are fighters who joined Jihad(جهاد) for no purpose other than financial reward of booty.

285
00:18:53,662 --> 00:18:57,795
If they were faced with the prospect of fighting without any financial compensation,

286
00:18:58,185 --> 00:18:59,725
they would not be willing to participate.

287
00:18:59,765 --> 00:19:04,212
So this really tells the difference between somebody who's fighting Jihad(جهاد) for the sake of Allah and booty.

288
00:19:04,474 --> 00:19:06,101
And somebody who's only fighting for booty.

289
00:19:06,466 --> 00:19:11,685
The one who is doing it for the sake of Allah, will still fight, even if there is no financial gain.

290
00:19:12,312 --> 00:19:14,717
However the one doing it for money,

291
00:19:16,042 --> 00:19:19,092
he is not going to fight unless they feel that they can make something out of it.

292
00:19:20,838 --> 00:19:25,844
For these, there is no reward whatsoever and if such a person dies, he is not a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

293
00:19:27,498 --> 00:19:28,696
NUMBER SEVEN, Recognition,

294
00:19:29,855 --> 00:19:33,901
there are some who Fight for fame and recognition, such a person is not a Mujahid(مُجَاهِد).

295
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:36,406
And if he dies, he is not the Shaheed(شَهِيد).

296
00:19:36,922 --> 00:19:41,661
He would also be one of the first to be thrown in the Hellfire, according to the Hadith(حديث).

297
00:19:42,550 --> 00:19:45,320
When we talked about preparation for Jihad(جهاد),

298
00:19:45,709 --> 00:19:48,963
this is one of the areas, where you want to prepare, yourself for.

299
00:19:49,622 --> 00:19:59,400
You want to get into that stage, where you fight off the urge of being known as a pious person.

300
00:20:01,192 --> 00:20:05,976
And you apply that to the other Ibadaat(عبادات).

301
00:20:06,064 --> 00:20:14,026
So that When the issue of Jihad(جهاد) does come up and the opportunity of Shahadah(شَهَادَة) opens up for you,

302
00:20:14,415 --> 00:20:18,566
you have already trained yourself on other ibadaat(عبادات), so that you're ready for this.

303
00:20:20,090 --> 00:20:21,433
It doesn't take you by surprise.

304
00:20:23,139 --> 00:20:30,052
So you've already Trained yourself, made Riyadha(رياضة) Tamreed( تمريد) that when it comes to Qiyam-Ul-lail(قيام اليل),

305
00:20:30,105 --> 00:20:33,905
when it comes to Nafaqa(نفقة), you would do some of these are Ibadaat(عبادات) in secret.

306
00:20:34,889 --> 00:20:38,641
Just for the sake of Allah, not try to let anybody know about it, even your wife.

307
00:20:39,151 --> 00:20:43,222
Because sometimes you assume that your wife is not really somebody else.

308
00:20:45,287 --> 00:20:50,679
And you forget that maybe sometimes the most important person that you would want to impress is your wife,

309
00:20:51,287 --> 00:20:52,271
more than anybody else.

310
00:20:53,224 --> 00:20:57,711
So there are some areas where you want to even conceal from the closest people to you.

311
00:20:58,449 --> 00:21:00,275
Your wife, your children, your parents.

312
00:21:01,005 --> 00:21:04,227
You do some nafaqat(نفقات) where nobody knows about it, nobody but you and Allah.

313
00:21:04,322 --> 00:21:06,194
At all even your left hand doesn't know about it.

314
00:21:07,202 --> 00:21:11,996
You do some Salah(صلاة) at the Joaf Al-Lail(جوف اليل), middle of the night, nobody knows about it.

315
00:21:12,567 --> 00:21:18,155
Get yourself trained to doing Ibadaat(عبادات) asking for no credit or recognition except for Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

316
00:21:19,212 --> 00:21:22,324
and to satisfy that human need of recognition.

317
00:21:22,744 --> 00:21:26,739
Always keep in mind that there is somebody watching you that's Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

318
00:21:27,667 --> 00:21:29,873
And He is really the One, that you want to please.

319
00:21:31,968 --> 00:21:37,195
Now how would it feel for your name to be mentioned on BBC and CNN,

320
00:21:37,275 --> 00:21:39,362
you're Praised and they say the best things about you.

321
00:21:39,798 --> 00:21:41,028
It feels good! You're famous!

322
00:21:42,108 --> 00:21:42,469
Right?

323
00:21:43,753 --> 00:21:47,532
And the Newspapers are writing about how such a fabulous person you are.

324
00:21:48,127 --> 00:21:50,636
I mean your head will become so big that day,

325
00:21:51,243 --> 00:21:54,301
but keep in mind that when you mention the name of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,

326
00:21:54,758 --> 00:21:58,232
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: Allah will mention your name in a better gathering.

327
00:21:59,446 --> 00:22:04,022
It's not BBC or CNN or it's not front page on newspaper,

328
00:22:04,553 --> 00:22:07,816
your name will be mentioned in front of the angels of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

329
00:22:09,252 --> 00:22:14,378
So, that recognition is there, you just need to channel it, in the right direction,

330
00:22:15,255 --> 00:22:20,176
be recognize it, in front of the angels, be recognize in front of the Hoor-Ul-Ain(حورالعين) if you want, be recognized…

331
00:22:20,969 --> 00:22:25,577
But forget about people because they're not gonna give you any good and they're not gonna harm you.

332
00:22:26,542 --> 00:22:29,225
Don't get yourself into a situation where you're not prepared and ready.

333
00:22:30,130 --> 00:22:35,361
So, be ready in terms of intension to face Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) and Shahadah(شَهَادَة).

334
00:22:37,226 --> 00:22:41,500
Now if a person has both intentions of fighting for the sake of Allah and recognition,

335
00:22:41,875 --> 00:22:44,811
then he would not be rewarded nor would he be punished.

336
00:22:45,327 --> 00:22:47,698
At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ) narrates that Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

337
00:22:49,452 --> 00:22:53,961
On the day of judgment when Allah will bring it together, the first and the last and announcement would be made.

338
00:22:55,792 --> 00:23:00,482
If someone associate someone else with Me, in the intention of their deeds,

339
00:23:00,887 --> 00:23:07,564
then let them seek the reward from whom they are associated because Allah accept no associates.

340
00:23:07,775 --> 00:23:08,592
That's very fair.!

341
00:23:10,203 --> 00:23:13,084
You did for somebody else. Go and claim the rewards from them.

342
00:23:14,235 --> 00:23:19,216
Because it's not for Allah, so don't ask for the reward to come from Allah.

343
00:23:20,327 --> 00:23:21,676
NUMBER EIGHT, Despair,

344
00:23:23,414 --> 00:23:32,390
there are some in order to die and get rid of their Painful weakness debt Poverty, despair, or life of difficulty.

345
00:23:32,758 --> 00:23:37,014
When they fight they are not thinking about pleasing Allah or raising high His word.

346
00:23:38,102 --> 00:23:40,755
For such a person it is possible to state

347
00:23:41,350 --> 00:23:45,661
that he is not considered the Shaheed(شَهِيد) because it Wasn't Jihad(جهاد) Done For the sake of Allah.

348
00:23:47,232 --> 00:23:52,629
One can also argue that he is Shaheed(شَهِيد) because he made sure that he doesn't, take away his life,

349
00:23:52,970 --> 00:23:56,587
except in that manner i.e. fighting the enemies of Allah.

350
00:23:57,301 --> 00:24:04,705
So if he could have faced death by the hands of armed robbers for example, or illness, he wouldn't have opted for it.

351
00:24:05,617 --> 00:24:06,586
 You get the point here.

352
00:24:08,133 --> 00:24:13,302
I would be more inclined to adopt the second view that he is in fact, a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

353
00:24:13,429 --> 00:24:16,766
Even though he is nowhere close to the sincere martyrs.

354
00:24:17,294 --> 00:24:18,040
So for example,

355
00:24:18,921 --> 00:24:27,389
in a martyrdom operation, somebody is doing it, because they have given up on living.

356
00:24:28,675 --> 00:24:33,718
So someone has given up on living and they decide to go and blow themselves up.

357
00:24:35,202 --> 00:24:36,535
Is this a Shahadah(شَهَادَة) or not?

358
00:24:37,139 --> 00:24:39,123
One of you would argue that it's not a Shahadah(شَهَادَة)

359
00:24:39,163 --> 00:24:42,663
because the reason it was done out of despair giving up his living.

360
00:24:43,243 --> 00:24:48,662
The other argument is that it is a Shahadah(شَهَادَة), because they didn't just swallow some pills and die at home.

361
00:24:49,548 --> 00:24:51,484
They went and harmed the enemy.

362
00:24:52,175 --> 00:24:55,542
However If somebody is doing it for the sake of Allah then it's clearly Shahadah(شَهَادَة).

363
00:24:55,998 --> 00:25:00,218
It's only this situation, where it's due to despair that they're taking that step.

364
00:25:01,768 --> 00:25:05,382
So these are the eight intentions that Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) mentions.

365
00:25:06,262 --> 00:25:08,254
RULINGS ON BEING PAID FOR FIGHTING,

366
00:25:09,317 --> 00:25:13,031
Scholars differs on the ruling of taking a payment in exchange of Jihad(جهاد).

367
00:25:13,690 --> 00:25:16,021
Some allow it, while others prohibit it.

368
00:25:17,198 --> 00:25:23,490
The ones who, allowed it, require that the payments should not be a conditions set by the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد).

369
00:25:24,458 --> 00:25:27,969
So if the payment is with held, the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) should still be willing to fight.

370
00:25:28,906 --> 00:25:36,082
If that's not the case, then the intention of fighter is merely the worldly compensation rather than for the sake of Allah.

371
00:25:37,685 --> 00:25:41,071
If a person only takes the payment because of their poverty,

372
00:25:41,415 --> 00:25:43,709
and they cannot make Jihad(جهاد) without such a payment,

373
00:25:44,256 --> 00:25:47,643
then there is no problem with the intention of such a person.

374
00:25:48,547 --> 00:25:54,755
And with the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) today, Yani(يعني) most of them are not really financing themselves.

375
00:25:54,866 --> 00:25:56,392
They're being paid to do it.

376
00:25:56,937 --> 00:26:01,674
Their food is covered, their lodging is covered and that's payment, that means payment.

377
00:26:03,071 --> 00:26:05,039
You know, we shouldn't only think of payments as been a salary.

378
00:26:06,063 --> 00:26:09,029
When you are in a camp, you're not really Paying for your food or your lodging.

379
00:26:09,831 --> 00:26:10,680
It's all taken care of.

380
00:26:11,141 --> 00:26:14,831
So it will be included, what Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) is saying here.

381
00:26:15,569 --> 00:26:18,545
Now it is allowed to take that payment.

382
00:26:19,108 --> 00:26:23,236
Because they are doing it for the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

383
00:26:23,465 --> 00:26:26,136
but if somebody is there, just to take advantage of the free food

384
00:26:26,977 --> 00:26:29,925
and lodging then that would be a problem in the intention.

385
00:26:36,115 --> 00:26:37,021
The Messenger of Allah said

386
00:26:37,061 --> 00:26:43,239
the fighter would get his reward while the one who finance the fighter would get his reward plus the reward of the fighter.

387
00:26:43,641 --> 00:26:45,221
So there is somebody paying for this fighter,

388
00:26:45,911 --> 00:26:47,427
ومَنْ جهَّزَ غَازِيًا فقد فَقَدْ غَزَا

389
00:26:47,815 --> 00:26:48,960
There's somebody paying for that.

390
00:26:50,024 --> 00:26:53,813
Seeking recognition in Jihad(جهاد) after starting it with a sincere intentions.

391
00:26:55,318 --> 00:26:56,490
So the beginning was right.

392
00:26:57,291 --> 00:27:01,732
You came back and now the intention is changing.

393
00:27:04,368 --> 00:27:06,657
You want to show off and want people to know about it.

394
00:27:06,800 --> 00:27:08,531
But when it was done originally, it was fine.

395
00:27:09,277 --> 00:27:11,039
What happens in this situations.

396
00:27:11,531 --> 00:27:12,370
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says:

397
00:27:12,799 --> 00:27:17,239
The Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) may have the right intention throughout his Jihad(جهاد), until the battle is over.

398
00:27:17,632 --> 00:27:22,913
But after that he might feel the urge to speak about his Jihad(جهاد) to people who didn't attend it.

399
00:27:23,374 --> 00:27:25,731
In order to have them know that he is Mujahid(مُجَاهِد).

400
00:27:26,532 --> 00:27:31,748
Or he might narrate stories intended to display his courage and skill in fighting.

401
00:27:33,145 --> 00:27:36,498
There are references that such an act destroys his reward.

402
00:27:38,162 --> 00:27:42,213
A man came to the Messenger of Allah and told him I have been fasting every day.

403
00:27:43,098 --> 00:27:47,126
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him neither did you fast nor did you break your fast.

404
00:27:48,002 --> 00:27:49,726
ما عصمت ولا افركت

405
00:27:50,804 --> 00:27:53,642
This man came to Rasool Ullah and said: I'm fasting every day.

406
00:27:53,833 --> 00:27:56,965
he's very happy about it, Rasul Ullah I'm fasting every day.

407
00:27:57,840 --> 00:28:00,921
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: You didn't fast and you didn't break you fast.

408
00:28:01,390 --> 00:28:04,834
He didn’t fast meaning you're not gonna get credit for that, because you were bragging

409
00:28:05,205 --> 00:28:08,054
and you didn't break your fast because you've only deprived yourself of food.

410
00:28:09,149 --> 00:28:14,366
Therefore a person should not revealed to others, his Jihad(جهاد)

411
00:28:15,213 --> 00:28:19,475
on that sense any of his good deeds in order to preserve his reward.

412
00:28:20,314 --> 00:28:23,117
But if there is a benefit in him talking about his Jihad(جهاد),

413
00:28:23,532 --> 00:28:28,619
like encouraging others or strengthening their hearts then that is allowed.

414
00:28:28,659 --> 00:28:32,633
As long as his an intention is the benefit and not to show off.

415
00:28:33,196 --> 00:28:36,203
So it's clear here that sometimes there's a benefit in telling the stories.

416
00:28:37,465 --> 00:28:40,955
And some people are looked up to, therefore they should tell them stories.

417
00:28:43,037 --> 00:28:47,396
A Mujahid(مُجَاهِد), who goes on to Jihad(جهاد) and dies without fighting is a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

418
00:28:49,166 --> 00:28:49,898
Allah says,

419
00:28:50,444 --> 00:28:54,603
وَمَن يُهاجِر في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ يَجِد فِي الأَرضِ مُراغَمًا كَثيرًا وَسَعَةً ۚ

420
00:28:55,032 --> 00:28:58,865
وَمَن يَخرُج مِن بَيتِهِ مُهاجِرًا إِلَى اللَّهِ وَرَسولِهِ ثُمَّ يُدرِكهُ المَوتُ

421
00:28:59,572 --> 00:29:03,286
فَقَد وَقَعَ أَجرُهُ عَلَى اللَّهِ ۗ وَكانَ اللَّهُ غَفورًا رَحيمًا۞

422
00:29:04,816 --> 00:29:11,413
And whoever emigrates for the cause of Allah, he will find on the earth many alternative locations in abundance

423
00:29:12,383 --> 00:29:18,062
and whoever leaves his home as an immigrant to Allah and His messenger and then death over takes him.

424
00:29:18,533 --> 00:29:22,019
His reward has already become incumbent upon Allah

425
00:29:22,455 --> 00:29:24,186
and Allah is ever forgiving and merciful.

426
00:29:24,305 --> 00:29:25,812
Al-Nisa(ألنساء) Verse 100.

427
00:29:27,360 --> 00:29:29,298
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) narrated Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

428
00:29:29,838 --> 00:29:35,912
The likeliness of Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) is like the one, who's praying and fasting without taking a break from praying and fasting,

429
00:29:36,359 --> 00:29:39,402
until he returns back to his family with booty or reward

430
00:29:39,950 --> 00:29:43,414
or Allah would take his soul away and enter him into paradise.

431
00:29:44,489 --> 00:29:46,938
Ibn Haban(إبن حبَّان), Bukhari(بخاريْ), Muslim(ألمسلم)  and An-Nasai(ألنَّسائ).

432
00:29:47,652 --> 00:29:49,721
Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) also narrates that Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

433
00:29:49,781 --> 00:29:50,989
Who are these Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء)?

434
00:29:52,255 --> 00:29:55,300
The companion said, the ones, who are killed in the path of Allah.

435
00:29:55,625 --> 00:29:56,695
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

436
00:29:56,995 --> 00:29:59,275
Then the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) in my nation are but a few.

437
00:30:00,357 --> 00:30:02,560
But the one, who was killed in the path of Allah is a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

438
00:30:03,303 --> 00:30:05,369
The one who dies in the path of Allah is a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

439
00:30:06,030 --> 00:30:10,556
So If you die, you are also a Shaheed(شَهِيد) as long as you are in the path of Allah.

440
00:30:10,859 --> 00:30:13,413
The One who falls off his mount, in the path of Allah is a Shaheed(شَهِيد),

441
00:30:13,882 --> 00:30:15,891
the one, who drowns in the path of Allah is Shaheed(شَهِيد).

442
00:30:16,328 --> 00:30:18,915
The one who dies in a plague in the path of Allah is the Shaheed(شَهِيد),

443
00:30:19,312 --> 00:30:23,719
the one who dies of an internal illness in the path of Allah is a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

444
00:30:25,091 --> 00:30:27,996
Ibn Abi Shaibah(إبن أبي شيبة), Abu Daud(أبوداؤد), An-Nasae(ألنسائ) and Ibn Majah(إبن ماجة).

445
00:30:28,956 --> 00:30:34,631
Sabura Bin Al-Faqih(صبورة بن ألفاكه) narrates I heard the Messenger of Allah say,

446
00:30:34,726 --> 00:30:39,932
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) has intercepted the son of Adam(آدَم) on his path towards Islam and told him:

447
00:30:40,737 --> 00:30:45,115
Are you going to become a Muslim and leave your heritage and the religion of your forefathers?

448
00:30:45,877 --> 00:30:50,335
The son of Adam(آدَم) disobeyed to him and became a Muslim and he was forgiven.

449
00:30:51,423 --> 00:30:54,383
Then Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) sat for him on his path to Hijrah(هجرة) and he told him:

450
00:30:54,954 --> 00:30:57,276
Do you make Hijrah(هجرة) and leave behind your home and land.?

451
00:30:58,113 --> 00:30:59,624
He disobeyed him and made Hijrah(هجرة).

452
00:31:00,267 --> 00:31:02,918
He then sat for him on his path towards Jihad(جهاد) and told him:

453
00:31:03,394 --> 00:31:06,744
Are you going to fight and it is an exhaustion of yourself and wealth.

454
00:31:07,736 --> 00:31:12,157
You would go to kill and would be killed and then your wife would be taken and the wealth divided.?

455
00:31:13,022 --> 00:31:15,387
The son of Adam(آدَم) disobeyed him and went on Jihad(جهاد).

456
00:31:16,054 --> 00:31:17,286
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

457
00:31:17,742 --> 00:31:22,129
Whoever does that it is incumbent upon Allah to admit him to paradise.

458
00:31:22,758 --> 00:31:27,079
Or if he dies by his animals striking him, he would go to Paradise.

459
00:31:28,808 --> 00:31:30,362
Rawah-O-Ahmad(رواة أحمد) and it is Hasan(حسن).

460
00:31:32,768 --> 00:31:36,502
Some scholars consider the status of the one, who's killed in the path of Allah

461
00:31:36,939 --> 00:31:40,007
and the one, who dies in the path of Allah to be equal.

462
00:31:40,843 --> 00:31:42,968
They are equal in martyrdom and reward.

463
00:31:43,667 --> 00:31:45,529
But the stronger opinion is that they're not.

464
00:31:46,619 --> 00:31:51,643
There's a difference between the one, who is killed and the one, who dies a natural death in the path of Allah.

465
00:31:51,731 --> 00:31:56,544
Obviously, the one who was killed has a higher status is preferred in a few ways.

466
00:31:57,306 --> 00:32:00,979
Ibn Haban(إبن حبَّان) narrates, Rasool Allah ﷺ was asked about the best Jihad(جهاد).

467
00:32:01,487 --> 00:32:06,070
He said: The best Jihad(جهاد) is the one in which your horse is slain and your blood is spilled.

468
00:32:06,693 --> 00:32:08,892
So, the one who was killed has practiced the best Jihad(جهاد).

469
00:32:09,558 --> 00:32:12,783
The dead is called dead even if he dies in the path of Allah,

470
00:32:13,128 --> 00:32:16,382
while the Shaheed(شَهِيد) is not considered to be dead, according to the Ayah(آية),

471
00:32:17,668 --> 00:32:24,268
وَلا تَحسَبَنَّ الَّذينَ قُتِلوا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ أَمواتًا ۚ

472
00:32:24,788 --> 00:32:29,287
بَل أَحياءٌ عِندَ رَبِّهِم يُرزَقونَ۞

473
00:32:29,614 --> 00:32:33,597
And do not say about those who are killed in the way of Allah they are dead,

474
00:32:33,952 --> 00:32:36,277
rather say they are alive but you perceive not.

475
00:32:36,674 --> 00:32:40,464
These shouldn't be numbered, but somehow the numberings disappeared,

476
00:32:41,654 --> 00:32:42,454
it should be number Two.

477
00:32:43,582 --> 00:32:46,238
The dead is called dead, this is number two.

478
00:32:47,200 --> 00:32:48,219
NUMBER THREE,

479
00:32:50,065 --> 00:32:54,994
the killed would have his injuries witness for him on the Day of Judgment.

480
00:32:55,565 --> 00:32:58,806
The injuries would gosh with Blood that smells like musk.

481
00:32:59,414 --> 00:33:00,144
NUMBER FOUR,

482
00:33:02,454 --> 00:33:08,541
the killed in the path of Allah will desire to come back to this world again and again, to be killed in the path of Allah.

483
00:33:09,025 --> 00:33:12,366
That does not happen with the one, who dies a natural death in the path of Allah.

484
00:33:13,138 --> 00:33:15,392
In Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم), Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

485
00:33:16,123 --> 00:33:21,889
There's no soul that dies and faces reward from Allah, that would be pleased to go back to this world,

486
00:33:22,392 --> 00:33:28,530
even if it would be given the World and  Everything in it except For Shaheed(شَهِيد),

487
00:33:29,008 --> 00:33:33,328
he wishes to come back to this world in order to be killed again in the path of Allah.

488
00:33:33,786 --> 00:33:37,838
That is because of the great reward he sees given to the Shaheed(شَهِيد).

489
00:33:38,410 --> 00:33:41,183
Being killed in the path of Allah forgives all sins.

490
00:33:41,815 --> 00:33:43,585
That is not the case with natural death.

491
00:33:44,053 --> 00:33:45,202
So this is number five.

492
00:33:46,508 --> 00:33:47,239
Number Six,

493
00:33:48,778 --> 00:33:54,087
The one dies in the path of Allah is prayed on, but the one Killed there's no prayer of Janazah(جنازة) offered.

494
00:33:54,461 --> 00:33:57,168
Because prayer is performed to ask Allah to forgive the dead.

495
00:33:57,596 --> 00:34:00,406
And since the Shaheed(شَهِيد) already has his sins forgiven,

496
00:34:00,771 --> 00:34:02,112
why offer a prayer for him?

497
00:34:07,360 --> 00:34:12,466
The next chapter is on martyrdom,

498
00:34:12,974 --> 00:34:13,641
Shahadah(شَهَادَة),

499
00:34:14,617 --> 00:34:16,147
asking for martyrdom and getting it.

500
00:34:17,553 --> 00:34:23,081
Allah has made it mandatory on us to ask him in every prayer to be guided to the straight path.

501
00:34:23,680 --> 00:34:26,896
The path of those, whom Allah has bestowed His favor on.

502
00:34:28,124 --> 00:34:29,116
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

503
00:34:29,204 --> 00:34:30,959
اهدِنَا الصِّراطَ المُستَقيمَ۞

504
00:34:31,039 --> 00:34:33,060
It is farz(فرض) to recite this.

505
00:34:33,140 --> 00:34:33,546
Righ!

506
00:34:34,123 --> 00:34:38,691
You say at 17 times, Surat Fatiha(سورة ألفاتحه), it is farz(فرض) to recite Surat Fatiha(سورة ألفاتحه).

507
00:34:41,080 --> 00:34:46,492
There is no other part of Qur'an that's Farz(فرض) to recite except Fatiha(فاتحه) its Farz Ain(فرض عين).

508
00:34:46,794 --> 00:34:48,238
Everybody has to recite Al-Fatiha(ألفاتحه).

509
00:34:48,952 --> 00:34:52,104
Because you have to do it, in every Raka'ah(ركعة) of Salah(صلاة), and the essence of Fatiha(فاتحه) is,

510
00:34:52,184 --> 00:34:53,382
اهدِنَا الصِّراطَ المُستَقيمَ۞

511
00:34:53,422 --> 00:34:54,394
Guide us through the straight path.

512
00:34:56,307 --> 00:34:56,974
And then Allah says:

513
00:34:57,045 --> 00:34:58,693
صِراطَ الَّذينَ أَنعَمتَ عَلَيهِم

514
00:34:58,974 --> 00:35:02,203
The path of those, who have bestowed your favor upon.

515
00:35:03,116 --> 00:35:04,195
Now, who are these?

516
00:35:05,521 --> 00:35:08,441
You're asking Allah to guide you to the straight path, the path of those.

517
00:35:08,886 --> 00:35:09,887
أنعم الله علينا

518
00:35:10,967 --> 00:35:12,658
Allah talks about them in Surat An-Nisa(سورة ألنساء)

519
00:35:12,867 --> 00:35:17,992
and gives us a definition of the ones, whom Allah bestowed His favor on.

520
00:35:18,931 --> 00:35:23,946
وَمَن يُطِعِ اللَّهَ وَالرَّسولَ فَأُولٰئِكَ مَعَ الَّذينَ أَنعَمَ اللَّهُ عَلَيهِم

521
00:35:24,266 --> 00:35:31,217
مِنَ النَّبِيّينَ وَالصِّدّيقينَ وَالشُّهَداءِ وَالصّالِحينَ ۚ وَحَسُنَ أُولٰئِكَ رَفيقًا۞

522
00:35:31,836 --> 00:35:32,906
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

523
00:35:34,733 --> 00:35:37,972
And who so ever obeys Allah and the messenger,

524
00:35:38,218 --> 00:35:43,895
those will be with the ones upon Allah has bestowed favor of the prophets,

525
00:35:44,300 --> 00:35:49,665
the steadfast affirmers of the truth, As-Sidiqeen(ألصديقين), the martyrs the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء), and the righteous.

526
00:35:51,372 --> 00:35:55,261
So we need to fall into one of these categories, obviously with in An-Nabuwa(ألنبوة).

527
00:35:56,219 --> 00:35:57,147
That's not for us.

528
00:35:57,536 --> 00:36:00,986
So we have Sidiqeen(صديقين), Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) and Saliheen(صالحين).

529
00:36:03,533 --> 00:36:07,255
Sidiqeen(صديقين), is the highest, Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) next and then Saliheen(صالحين).

530
00:36:08,478 --> 00:36:11,277
Sahil Ibn Haneef(سهل إبن حنيف) narrates: Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

531
00:36:11,833 --> 00:36:19,183
Whoever asked Allah for martyrdom earnestly, Allah will elevate him to the level of martyrs, even if he dies on his bed.

532
00:36:21,120 --> 00:36:22,928
ومات على فراشه

533
00:36:23,602 --> 00:36:24,301
Number two,

534
00:36:25,269 --> 00:36:26,839
Amr Bin Saad(عمر بن سعد) narrates:

535
00:36:27,229 --> 00:36:32,001
A man came to pray, while the prophet was praying, and he said: Oh Allah,

536
00:36:32,366 --> 00:36:36,776
I asked you for the best thing you give to your righteous servants,

537
00:36:37,366 --> 00:36:39,802
when Rasool Allah ﷺ finished prayer he turned and said:

538
00:36:40,244 --> 00:36:42,545
Who was the one speaking before, the man said:

539
00:36:42,903 --> 00:36:44,291
Me, O Messenger of Allah,

540
00:36:44,704 --> 00:36:45,875
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

541
00:36:46,133 --> 00:36:49,308
Then your horse would be slain, and you would be a martyr.

542
00:36:50,114 --> 00:36:52,014
You asked for the best thing, that's the best thing,

543
00:36:53,933 --> 00:36:58,386
Ibn Habban(إبن حبَّان) and Al Hakim(ألحَاكِم), Abu Ya'al(أبويعلى), Al-Bazzar(ألبزار), As-Sahaha Az-Zahbi( ألصحاح الذهبي).

544
00:36:58,762 --> 00:37:00,948
 Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) narrated Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

545
00:37:01,446 --> 00:37:07,168
Whoever goes out in His cause with no purpose but to fight for His sake,

546
00:37:07,544 --> 00:37:09,698
 and believing in Him and His Messengers,

547
00:37:10,142 --> 00:37:15,552
Allah will guarantee for him to either enter him into paradise or to return him home with rewards or booties.

548
00:37:16,337 --> 00:37:18,992
In the name of whom Muhammad(محمد) soul is in His hand,

549
00:37:19,505 --> 00:37:21,515
whoever is injured in the path of Allah,

550
00:37:21,890 --> 00:37:27,735
the injury would come on the Day of Judgment, as it was in this world, the color is that of blood and the smell is that of musk.

551
00:37:29,481 --> 00:37:33,436
In the name of Whom Muhammad(محمد) soul in His hand.

552
00:37:34,006 --> 00:37:36,374
If it wasn't for making things difficult on Muslims,

553
00:37:36,735 --> 00:37:41,036
I wouldn't have stayed behind any army, leaving in the path of Allah.

554
00:37:41,432 --> 00:37:44,634
But I'm unable to find sustenance for the Muslims who stay behind,

555
00:37:45,059 --> 00:37:49,609
and they have nothing, and it is difficult on them for me to go while leaving them behind.

556
00:37:50,131 --> 00:37:52,689
In the name of Whom Muhammad(محمد) Soul is in His hand,

557
00:37:53,258 --> 00:37:59,785
I wish I could fight in the Cause of Allah and then be killed, and then fight and then be killed, and then fight, then be killed.

558
00:38:00,103 --> 00:38:07,720
If Rasool Allah ﷺ wants that status of Shahadah(شَهَادَة), then we should be begging, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ for it.

559
00:38:09,639 --> 00:38:14,763
This is the month of Ramadan(رمضان), so pray to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ earnestly to grant you this level.

560
00:38:15,867 --> 00:38:26,720
Because Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), I remember, in witr(وتر) in Dua Al-Qanoot(دعا قنوت) in the Masjid(مسجد).

561
00:38:28,062 --> 00:38:35,379
When the Imam(اِمَام) is making Dua(دُعَا) everybody's saying Ameen(آمين) so loud.

562
00:38:35,962 --> 00:38:38,329
And then when the Imam(اِمَام) says O Allah give us Shahadah(شَهَادَة),

563
00:38:39,901 --> 00:38:41,273
the volume goes down.

564
00:38:42,558 --> 00:38:44,592
Half of the people are not even saying Ameen(آمين).

565
00:38:46,779 --> 00:38:52,003
So this Shahadah(شَهَادَة) is the thing that we should be asking Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ Begging Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to give us,

566
00:38:52,090 --> 00:38:53,937
because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ said:

567
00:38:53,977 --> 00:38:54,868
ويتخذ منكم شهدآء

568
00:38:55,192 --> 00:38:55,935
He chooses.

569
00:38:56,627 --> 00:38:59,059
It is a choice from Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ it's not given to everybody.

570
00:39:00,661 --> 00:39:04,016
Jabir(جابر) narrated that he heard the Prophet mentioned the martyrs of Uhud(أحَد).

571
00:39:04,096 --> 00:39:06,685
Rasool Allah ﷺ was talking about the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) of Uhud(أحَد) and then he said:

572
00:39:07,226 --> 00:39:11,396
I wish, I have departed with my companions under that mountain, I wish I was with them.

573
00:39:12,370 --> 00:39:16,755
 Is'haq Bin Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(أسحاق بن سعد إبن أبي وقاص) narrated that his father told him.

574
00:39:17,542 --> 00:39:20,420
This is a wonderful story.

575
00:39:22,577 --> 00:39:26,321
Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعد إبن أبي وقاص) told his son.

576
00:39:29,047 --> 00:39:33,094
So the son of Saad(سعد) is telling his grandson,

577
00:39:33,599 --> 00:39:35,915
about the father, about the story of Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعد إبن أبي وقاص).

578
00:39:35,961 --> 00:39:39,394
He told him that Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش) told him before the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

579
00:39:39,762 --> 00:39:40,829
Let's go and make Dua(دُعَا)!

580
00:39:41,803 --> 00:39:46,424
 So, this is before the battle, these are two friends Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعد إبن أبي وقاص) and Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش),

581
00:39:46,715 --> 00:39:47,786
they said: Let's go and make Dua(دُعَا).

582
00:39:48,104 --> 00:39:48,996
So they go and make Dua(دعاء)

583
00:39:51,100 --> 00:39:53,037
So Saad(سعد) went first.

584
00:39:53,725 --> 00:39:57,076
He said: Oh Allah, if we meet our enemy tomorrow.

585
00:39:57,634 --> 00:40:03,071
Then lets me face a tough fighter, so I can fight him for Your sake and he can fight me.

586
00:40:03,607 --> 00:40:05,472
Then let me defeat him and kill him.

587
00:40:06,755 --> 00:40:08,683
And then now Abdullah(عبدالله)'s turn to make Dua(دُعَا).

588
00:40:09,450 --> 00:40:13,659
So Abdullah(عبدالله) said: Oh Allah, let me face a tough fighter,

589
00:40:14,258 --> 00:40:17,099
so I can fight him for Your sake and he can fight me.

590
00:40:17,781 --> 00:40:21,049
Let him kill me, and then cut my nose and ears.

591
00:40:21,789 --> 00:40:26,885
So when I meet you, you would ask me, Oh AbdAllah(عبدالله), why were your nose and ears cut off.

592
00:40:27,582 --> 00:40:31,377
I would reply, they were cut off for Your sake, and for Your Messenger.

593
00:40:32,614 --> 00:40:35,022
And then you would say: Yes! You spoke the truth.

594
00:40:35,736 --> 00:40:38,408
Is'haq Bin Saad(إسحاق بن سعد) said: My father said: Oh my son.

595
00:40:38,689 --> 00:40:40,999
The prayer of Abdullah(عبدالله) was better than mine.

596
00:40:41,335 --> 00:40:45,832
I found him at the end of the day with his nose and ears, tied in a string.

597
00:40:47,408 --> 00:40:51,211
Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش) was killed and his nose and ears were cut,

598
00:40:51,690 --> 00:40:53,360
and they found them tied in the string.

599
00:40:54,543 --> 00:40:57,533
It is in Al Hakim(ألحَاكِم) authenticated by Az-Zahbi(ألذهبي).

600
00:41:00,787 --> 00:41:04,857
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) used to say: Oh Allah, I asked you for martyrdom,

601
00:41:06,021 --> 00:41:07,265
in the city of your prophet.

602
00:41:07,887 --> 00:41:08,707
And this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

603
00:41:08,912 --> 00:41:10,844
Hafsa(حفصه), the daughter of Umar(عُمَر)

604
00:41:11,343 --> 00:41:14,916
would go to her father and would say, Oh Father: How could you become a Shaheed(شَهِيد) in Madina?

605
00:41:15,622 --> 00:41:18,327
Madina is the capital of Islam, there is no enemy that is going to come here.

606
00:41:19,227 --> 00:41:25,216
So she said: I used to wonder, I mean, you asked for Shahadah(شَهَادَة) that's fine but in Madina,

607
00:41:25,706 --> 00:41:29,085
in the house of the believers, the capital of the Muslims.

608
00:41:30,560 --> 00:41:34,716
But the thing is to learn here from Umar(عُمَر), ask for what you want from Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

609
00:41:34,842 --> 00:41:36,779
Ask for it, whatever it is, ask for it!

610
00:41:38,241 --> 00:41:40,716
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) Allah brought Shahadah(شَهَادَة) to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

611
00:41:40,932 --> 00:41:44,631
straight, not only to Madina, but to the Masjid An-Nabwi(مسجد ألنبوي) and in Salat-Ul-Fajr(صلاة الفجر).

612
00:41:45,259 --> 00:41:47,228
He couldn't ask for anything better.

613
00:41:48,460 --> 00:41:55,189
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ sent him that man to kill him, because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ chose Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) to be a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

614
00:41:56,132 --> 00:41:58,840
Az-Zahbi(ألذهبي) narrated that the Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said:

615
00:41:59,283 --> 00:42:01,732
I was with my brother Hisham(هشام) at Yarmook(يرموك),

616
00:42:01,995 --> 00:42:05,624
and we spent our night praying that Allah blesses us with martyrdom.

617
00:42:06,031 --> 00:42:08,308
The next day my brother got it but I didn't.

618
00:42:10,888 --> 00:42:15,076
Anas(أنس) narrated the Messenger of Allah said: A man from Paradise will be asked by Allah.

619
00:42:15,747 --> 00:42:16,750
Oh son of Adam(آدَم):

620
00:42:17,570 --> 00:42:19,250
Are you satisfied with your dwelling?

621
00:42:19,647 --> 00:42:21,003
He will say: Oh my Lord.

622
00:42:21,413 --> 00:42:24,753
This is the greatest dwelling, Allah will say ask whatever you want.

623
00:42:25,467 --> 00:42:32,097
He will say: I asked that you take me back to Earth, so I can be killed for you 10 times.

624
00:42:32,997 --> 00:42:35,748
He says that when he sees the great status of martyrdom,

625
00:42:37,044 --> 00:42:42,140
then Allah will ask a man from hellfire, or son of Adam(آدَم), how do you find your dwelling?

626
00:42:42,847 --> 00:42:45,313
He would say Oh My lord, this is the worst dwelling.

627
00:42:46,347 --> 00:42:52,595
Allah ask him, would you then save yourself from it by paying the equivalent of the whole world filled with gold.

628
00:42:53,415 --> 00:42:54,738
He would say: Yes!

629
00:42:55,188 --> 00:42:56,832
Allah would tell him, you are lying.

630
00:42:57,301 --> 00:42:59,630
I asked you for less than that and you didn't do it.

631
00:43:00,489 --> 00:43:01,653
All what I ask you is for,

632
00:43:01,799 --> 00:43:02,646
لا اله الا الله

633
00:43:04,236 --> 00:43:10,229
If the people of paradise will desire martyrdom, even though they are already given the greatest blessings.

634
00:43:10,881 --> 00:43:12,726
Then How couldn't we ask for it.

635
00:43:13,295 --> 00:43:17,346
When we are living in the dwelling and sorrow, pain, deception and evil,

636
00:43:17,783 --> 00:43:21,674
and we don't even know whether we are heading for Paradise or hellfire.

637
00:43:23,229 --> 00:43:25,347
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said: I've already read the statement.

638
00:43:26,716 --> 00:43:32,022
If I were to marry a beautiful woman whom I love, or if I were given the good news of having a newborn son

639
00:43:32,458 --> 00:43:34,331
is less beloved and dear to my heart,

640
00:43:34,886 --> 00:43:40,098
than to be in a cold icy night in an army waiting to meet my enemy the next morning,

641
00:43:40,562 --> 00:43:42,194
I advise you to go in Jihad(جهاد).

642
00:43:42,720 --> 00:43:44,597
These were the words of Khalid(خالد) before his death.

643
00:43:45,184 --> 00:43:46,331
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) said:

644
00:43:48,328 --> 00:43:53,576
My father Umar(عُمَر) during the Battle of Uhud(أحَد) told his brother Zaed(زيد), Take my shield.

645
00:43:54,394 --> 00:43:57,560
Zaed(زيد) replied: I'm seeking martyrdom just like you are,

646
00:43:58,124 --> 00:44:00,755
and he refused to take it, they both ended up leaving it,

647
00:44:02,204 --> 00:44:03,743
Abu Naeem Al-Hilyar(ابو نعيم ألحلير).

648
00:44:04,878 --> 00:44:08,362
Zaed(زيد) was the older brother of Umar(عُمَر), he became Muslim before Umar(عُمَر).

649
00:44:09,108 --> 00:44:10,524
He was a very tall man.

650
00:44:11,334 --> 00:44:14,596
He sought after martyrdom during the Battle of Uhud(أحَد) but didn't get it.

651
00:44:15,342 --> 00:44:17,377
He lived past the Messenger of Allah,

652
00:44:17,535 --> 00:44:22,186
and during the battle of Yamamah(أليمامة), he was carrying the banner of the Muslim army.

653
00:44:22,885 --> 00:44:27,704
He continued marching forward with it, fighting his way with his sword until he was killed,

654
00:44:28,204 --> 00:44:29,188
and the banner fell down.

655
00:44:29,879 --> 00:44:32,799
It was later picked up by Salim(سالم) the servant of Abu Hudhaifah(أبوحذيفة).

656
00:44:33,506 --> 00:44:37,045
When the news of his death reached to Umar(عُمَر), he was extremely saddened by it.

657
00:44:38,124 --> 00:44:42,232
He said, My brother became a Muslim before me, and then won martyrdom before me.

658
00:44:42,831 --> 00:44:47,048
He would later say whenever the wind of the east blows, it would remind me of my brother Zaed(زيد).

659
00:44:48,563 --> 00:44:52,912
Umar(عُمَر) wasn't allowed to participate in the battle of Yarmook(يرموك),

660
00:44:54,928 --> 00:45:00,159
because Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) held him in Madina to be his advisor,

661
00:45:00,563 --> 00:45:01,770
I mean in Al-Yamamah(أليمامة),

662
00:45:02,501 --> 00:45:06,738
again Zaid(زيد) was older than Umar(عُمَر), he became Muslim before Umar(عُمَر) and he became a Shaheed(شَهِيد) before Umar(عُمَر),

663
00:45:07,477 --> 00:45:13,229
but because Umar(عُمَر) didn't join in Yamamah(يمامة).

664
00:45:13,826 --> 00:45:16,604
But his brother and son Abdullah(عبدالله), were there.

665
00:45:17,127 --> 00:45:23,162
I want you, especially those of you who are fathers again, I mean, think about how dearly you love your son

666
00:45:23,773 --> 00:45:24,832
and how much you care for them.

667
00:45:25,456 --> 00:45:28,026
When Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) came back from Al-Yamamah(أليمامة).

668
00:45:28,899 --> 00:45:31,627
And the news reached to Umar(عُمَر) that his brother was killed.

669
00:45:32,252 --> 00:45:38,915
Umar(عُمَر) loved Zaed(زيد) a lot, he loved him a lot, and he was very saddened by the news of his death.

670
00:45:39,557 --> 00:45:43,089
What was the response of Umar(عُمَر), when he saw Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) coming in, what do he tell him.?

671
00:45:45,867 --> 00:45:49,008
Welcome, my son. Al-Hamdulillah(ألحمدلله), you came back safe,

672
00:45:51,048 --> 00:45:55,293
Allah Ho Akbar(ألله أكبر) you didn't die, May Allah give you a longer life.

673
00:45:56,579 --> 00:45:59,476
When Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) came in, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) looked at him and said:

674
00:46:01,666 --> 00:46:04,189
How dare you show me your face,

675
00:46:05,251 --> 00:46:08,211
when your uncle died as a Shaheed(شَهِيد) and you didn't.

676
00:46:09,718 --> 00:46:13,211
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), look at the words of Umar(عُمَر) to his son Abdullah(عبدالله).

677
00:46:14,497 --> 00:46:18,127
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) said: Oh my father, I asked Allah to give me Shahadah(شَهَادَة),

678
00:46:19,066 --> 00:46:21,703
and my uncle asked for it, but he got it, but I didn't.

679
00:46:24,025 --> 00:46:27,458
Now Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) as it is said here,

680
00:46:28,319 --> 00:46:31,469
Whenever the wind would blow from the east, he would remember Zaed(زيد),

681
00:46:32,068 --> 00:46:34,530
it would bring him back the memories of his brother Zaid(زيد).

682
00:46:36,449 --> 00:46:40,487
Salah Bin Aqsam(صلاح بن أقصم) told his son, Oh my son go ahead and fight.

683
00:46:41,440 --> 00:46:46,083
His son went ahead and was killed, later on, Salah(صلاح) himself was killed.

684
00:46:46,962 --> 00:46:52,043
When the wife of Salah(صلاح) received the news of the death of both her husband and son.

685
00:46:52,662 --> 00:46:55,471
She told the women who came to give her their condolences.

686
00:46:56,266 --> 00:46:58,831
If you are coming to congratulate me then you're welcome.

687
00:46:59,512 --> 00:47:02,401
If you are here to give me condolences, then you must leave,

688
00:47:03,956 --> 00:47:08,258
Ibn-Al-Mubarak(إبن مبارك), Az-Zahbi(الذهبي), in Seerah Alam-Un-Nubula(سيروعلام النبلاء), Abu Naeem Al-Hilya(أبونعيم ألحلية)

689
00:47:08,671 --> 00:47:10,064
and Ibn Saad in Tabaqaat(طبقات سعد ).

690
00:47:12,120 --> 00:47:15,342
Saad Ibn Ibrahim(سعدإبن اِبْراهِيْم) narrates that during the Battle of Qadisiyah(قادسية)

691
00:47:15,382 --> 00:47:19,612
they passed by a man who had both his arms and both his legs cut off during the battle,

692
00:47:20,279 --> 00:47:22,468
rolling in his blood, and he was reciting,

693
00:47:22,691 --> 00:47:31,951
وَمَن يُطِعِ اللَّهَ وَالرَّسولَ فَأُولٰئِكَ مَعَ الَّذينَ أَنعَمَ اللَّهُ عَلَيهِم

694
00:47:32,642 --> 00:47:44,240
مَعَ الَّذينَ أَنعَمَ اللَّهُ عَلَيهِم مِنَ النَّبِيّينَ وَالصِّدّيقينَ وَالشُّهَداءِ وَالصّالِحينَ ۚ

695
00:47:44,913 --> 00:47:48,470
وَحَسُنَ أُولٰئِكَ رَفيقًا۞

696
00:47:48,747 --> 00:47:53,985
And whosoever obeys Allah and His Messenger, those will be with the ones upon whom Allah has bestowed favor

697
00:47:54,541 --> 00:47:59,275
of the prophets, the steadfast affirmers of truth, the martyrs and the righteous,

698
00:47:59,577 --> 00:48:01,677
and excellent are those as companions.

699
00:48:02,847 --> 00:48:05,782
They said: Who are you, he said the man from Ansaar(ألأنْصَار).

700
00:48:06,965 --> 00:48:08,719
The virtues of martyrdom.

701
00:48:09,116 --> 00:48:14,253
Martyrdom is a great blessing and a noble status that is not given except to the very fortunate.

702
00:48:15,261 --> 00:48:18,065
The martyrs are accompanying the prophets in paradise.

703
00:48:18,930 --> 00:48:23,533
And whosoever obeys Allah and the Messenger and recite this Ayah(آية) An-Nisa(ألنساء) Verse 69.

704
00:48:24,922 --> 00:48:28,969
The scholars have different views on why the martyr is called to Shaheed(شَهِيد).

705
00:48:29,294 --> 00:48:32,224
Shaheed(شَهِيد) in Arabic means witness, some of which are,

706
00:48:33,692 --> 00:48:34,379
NUMBER ONE,

707
00:48:35,541 --> 00:48:37,728
ألشهيدو من شهدالله له ورسوله

708
00:48:38,522 --> 00:48:43,215
Because Allah and His angels are witnesses that paradise is granted for such a person.

709
00:48:44,117 --> 00:48:48,043
They witness that paradise is granted for him, that's why he's called Shaheed(شَهِيد).

710
00:48:48,599 --> 00:48:50,254
Because Shaheed(شَهِيد) means witness.

711
00:48:51,305 --> 00:48:51,987
NUMBER TWO,

712
00:48:53,059 --> 00:48:57,263
because their souls witness paradise, this is the opinion of Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي),

713
00:48:58,010 --> 00:49:00,300
the souls of the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) are witnessing paradise.

714
00:49:00,962 --> 00:49:01,724
NUMBER THREE,

715
00:49:02,168 --> 00:49:07,648
because they are witnesses over the transaction between them and Allah mentioned in the verse.

716
00:49:08,068 --> 00:49:15,688
إِنَّ اللَّهَ اشتَرىٰ مِنَ المُؤمِنينَ أَنفُسَهُم وَأَموالَهُم

717
00:49:16,080 --> 00:49:21,040
وَأَموالَهُم بِأَنَّ لَهُمُ الجَنَّةَ ۚ

718
00:49:21,373 --> 00:49:28,502
يُقاتِلونَ في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ فَيَقتُلونَ وَيُقتَلونَ ۖ

719
00:49:28,797 --> 00:49:36,901
وَعدًا عَلَيهِ حَقًّا فِي التَّوراةِ وَالإِنجيلِ وَالقُرآنِ ۚ

720
00:49:37,147 --> 00:49:41,553
وَمَن أَوفىٰ بِعَهدِهِ مِنَ اللَّهِ ۚ

721
00:49:41,849 --> 00:49:47,292
فَاستَبشِروا بِبَيعِكُمُ الَّذي بايَعتُم بِهِ ۚ

722
00:49:47,579 --> 00:49:51,980
وَذٰلِكَ هُوَ الفَوزُ العَظيمُ۞

723
00:49:53,157 --> 00:50:00,229
Indeed Allah purchase from the believers their lives and their properties in exchange for that they will have paradise.

724
00:50:00,577 --> 00:50:03,807
They fight in the Cause of Allah. So they kill and are killed.

725
00:50:04,347 --> 00:50:09,067
It is a true promise binding upon him in the Torah(توراة) and the Gospel and the Qur'an

726
00:50:09,453 --> 00:50:11,747
and who is truer to his covenant than Allah.

727
00:50:12,128 --> 00:50:14,854
So rejoice in your transaction which you have contracted

728
00:50:15,199 --> 00:50:17,105
and is that which is the great attainment.

729
00:50:17,215 --> 00:50:18,001
At-Toba(التوبة) Verse 111.

730
00:50:19,255 --> 00:50:19,985
NUMBER FOUR,

731
00:50:20,499 --> 00:50:27,022
When the soul of the martyr leaves his body it witnesses the bounties, Allah has prepared for him.

732
00:50:27,510 --> 00:50:29,661
So these are the various meanings given to Ash-Shaheed(شَهِيد).

733
00:50:32,343 --> 00:50:34,546
Allah has bestowed on the Shaheed(شَهِيد) many bounties,

734
00:50:35,070 --> 00:50:37,301
one of which is the fact that the Shaheed(شَهِيد) is alive.

735
00:50:38,609 --> 00:50:45,231
وَلا تَحسَبَنَّ الَّذينَ قُتِلوا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ أَمواتًا ۚ

736
00:50:45,746 --> 00:50:50,228
بَل أَحياءٌ عِندَ رَبِّهِم يُرزَقونَ۞

737
00:50:50,683 --> 00:50:56,455
وَلا تَحسَبَنَّ الَّذينَ قُتِلوا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ أَمواتًا ۚ بَل أَحياءٌ عِندَ رَبِّهِم يُرزَقونَ۞

738
00:50:57,415 --> 00:51:00,063
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث) narrated by Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس),

739
00:51:00,143 --> 00:51:04,635
the martyrs are on the banks of a river next to the gates of paradise in the green dome,

740
00:51:05,550 --> 00:51:08,714
they received their provisions from paradise in the morning and night.

741
00:51:09,836 --> 00:51:11,450
And this is an authentic Hadith(حديث).

742
00:51:11,955 --> 00:51:17,623
So you find that different Hadith(حديث) mentioned different things about the souls of the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء),

743
00:51:19,108 --> 00:51:23,498
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says: Scholars interpreted the essence of the life of a martyr,

744
00:51:23,958 --> 00:51:26,740
Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) mentioned, the various views on the subject.

745
00:51:27,538 --> 00:51:32,218
Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) stated that the life of the Shaheed(شَهِيد), is in the literal sense,

746
00:51:32,915 --> 00:51:37,631
and that their bodies are dead, but their souls are not, just like all the believers,

747
00:51:37,819 --> 00:51:43,939
but the difference is that the Shaheed(شَهِيد) receives provisions from Paradise, while the rest of the believers don't.

748
00:51:44,526 --> 00:51:50,294
So every soul does retain consciousness, whether it is a Shaheed(شَهِيد) or non Shaheed(شَهِيد), Muslim or non Muslim,

749
00:51:51,866 --> 00:51:55,203
but the difference between the soul of the Shaheed(شَهِيد) and the soul of the believer,

750
00:51:55,737 --> 00:52:01,078
is that the soul of Shaheed(شَهِيد) is given provision there's Rizq(رزق) coming on, so they are alive.

751
00:52:04,038 --> 00:52:09,103
Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) say is the martyrs feed from the fruits of Paradise, but they are not actually in it.

752
00:52:09,746 --> 00:52:13,639
Others say that the souls of the martyrs are inside green birds in paradise.

753
00:52:14,393 --> 00:52:18,225
Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) adopts this view because it is supported by the sayings of the Prophet.

754
00:52:19,079 --> 00:52:25,370
Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) continues by saying that the Shaheed(شَهِيد) would receive the reward of fighting one battle every year,

755
00:52:25,801 --> 00:52:29,483
and he will also share in the rewards of every Jihad(جهاد) until the Day of Judgment.

756
00:52:30,392 --> 00:52:35,503
My view is that the life of the Shaheed(شَهِيد) is different, and it depends on the status of the Shaheed(شَهِيد),

757
00:52:36,384 --> 00:52:40,654
some Shaheed(شَهِيد)s would have their souls and the insides of birds of paradise.

758
00:52:41,091 --> 00:52:42,891
Flying wherever they want in paradise,

759
00:52:43,686 --> 00:52:47,265
others would be on the river just outside the gates of paradise,

760
00:52:47,797 --> 00:52:51,843
and they would receive their provisions every morning and night from inside paradise.

761
00:52:52,796 --> 00:52:56,470
The souls of others would be flying with the angels wherever they want,

762
00:52:57,002 --> 00:53:00,540
and others would be reclining on thrones, in Jannah(جنة).

763
00:53:01,026 --> 00:53:05,060
The Earth does not consume the bodies of the martyrs.

764
00:53:06,526 --> 00:53:08,774
The body of the Shaheed(شَهِيد) does not decompose.

765
00:53:09,369 --> 00:53:11,051
Abdul Rehman Bin Sa'sa(عبدالرحمن بن صعصعة) said:

766
00:53:11,361 --> 00:53:14,394
And Allah Alam(ألله أعلم), this is general for every Shaheed(شَهِيد) or some.

767
00:53:15,496 --> 00:53:17,081
Abdul Rehman Bin Sa'sa(عبدالرحمن بن صعصعة) said:

768
00:53:17,875 --> 00:53:21,925
I was told that Amr Bin Jamuah(عمروبن جموح) and Abdullah Bin Amr(عبدالله بن عمرو), both from Ansaar(ألأنْصَار),

769
00:53:22,740 --> 00:53:28,130
were martyred during the Battle of Uhud(أحَد) and the Messenger of Allah, placed them in the same grave.

770
00:53:29,870 --> 00:53:33,127
During the reign of Muawiya(معاويه) , the storm flooded the cemetery.

771
00:53:33,529 --> 00:53:37,790
So their grave was opened in order to change its location.

772
00:53:38,504 --> 00:53:42,714
When the grave was opened their bodies were found in tact as if they died yesterday.

773
00:53:42,976 --> 00:53:45,303
This occurred 46 years after their death.

774
00:53:46,119 --> 00:53:47,316
It was mentioned by Imam Malik(إمام مالك).

775
00:53:49,014 --> 00:53:52,853
The same incident is also referred to here, Jabir(جابر) narrates Muawiya(معاويه) said:

776
00:53:53,448 --> 00:53:58,874
Whoever has a dead person in this cemetery, the cemetery of the martyrs of Uhud(أحَد) should remove the remains,

777
00:53:59,313 --> 00:54:04,886
 because it's so it was a floodplain and it was flooded so some of the bodies were uncovered.

778
00:54:04,985 --> 00:54:06,783
So, Muawiya(معاويه) said: Move them to higher ground.

779
00:54:07,362 --> 00:54:07,966
Jabir(جابر) said:

780
00:54:08,331 --> 00:54:12,676
We pulled them out of their graves with tender bodies, as if they were alive.

781
00:54:13,249 --> 00:54:18,780
One of the bodies was hit by an axe in the leg, and blood dripped from the injury,

782
00:54:19,092 --> 00:54:20,803
we're talking about 46 years after they died.

783
00:54:23,116 --> 00:54:26,728
The son of Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) said: I went to the grave of my uncle Hamza(حمزه),

784
00:54:27,197 --> 00:54:29,813
and I retrieved his body and it didn't change.

785
00:54:32,149 --> 00:54:35,961
It was mentioned that the grave of the young man from the story of the trench.

786
00:54:38,333 --> 00:54:41,420
Let me retract, in the first incident.

787
00:54:42,238 --> 00:54:44,547
We have Amr Bin Jamooh(عمروبن جموح), and Abdullah Bin Amr(عبدالله بن عمرو).

788
00:54:45,746 --> 00:54:51,967
It says that one of them had his right hand under his cheek as if he was sleeping.

789
00:54:52,166 --> 00:54:56,372
When they described, they looked at him as if he was sleeping, he had his hand under his cheek.

790
00:54:57,078 --> 00:54:58,752
We're alking about 46 years after they died.

791
00:54:58,792 --> 00:55:07,455
It was mentioned that the grave of the young man from the story of the Trench, was found during the reign of Umar(عُمَر).

792
00:55:08,168 --> 00:55:12,411
The young man had his hand over his head in the place the arrow hit him.

793
00:55:15,704 --> 00:55:20,632
Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) stated that the people of Madina narrated that the wall of the grave of the Messenger of Allah collapsed

794
00:55:20,917 --> 00:55:22,934
during the reign of Al-Walid Bin Abdul Malik(ألوليد بن عبدالملك),

795
00:55:24,330 --> 00:55:26,613
when Umar Bin Abdulaziz(عمر بن عبدالعزيز) was the governor of Madina.

796
00:55:27,473 --> 00:55:29,467
When the wall collapsed the foot was uncovered

797
00:55:29,967 --> 00:55:34,154
and the people were terrified, thinking that it was a foot of the Messenger of Allah.

798
00:55:35,209 --> 00:55:40,330
The grandson of Umar(عُمَر) came and saw the foot and he said that it was the foot of his grandfather Umar(عُمَر),

799
00:55:41,026 --> 00:55:42,204
and Umar(عُمَر) died as a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

800
00:55:43,585 --> 00:55:48,214
If the martyr was considered to be alive, then there is no prayer for the dead performed for them.

801
00:55:48,966 --> 00:55:49,961
Guarding the washing,

802
00:55:50,540 --> 00:55:54,969
Imam Malik(إمام مالك), As-Shafie(ألشَّافعي) and Abu Hanifah(أبوحنيفه) say that the Shaheed(شَهِيد) shouldn't be washed.

803
00:55:55,786 --> 00:55:59,717
In Al-Bukhari(ألبخاريْ) the Messenger of Allah ordered that the martyrs of Uhud(أحَد) be buried without any washing,

804
00:55:59,797 --> 00:56:01,189
without prayer of Janazah(جنازة).

805
00:56:02,769 --> 00:56:07,311
The reason, the martyrs are not washed because their blood would witness for them on the day of judgment.

806
00:56:08,606 --> 00:56:11,615
Al-Hasan(ألحسن) and Ibn Musayyib(إبن مصيب) say that the Shaheed(شَهِيد) should be washed,

807
00:56:11,773 --> 00:56:14,003
but the stronger opinion is that they are not washed.

808
00:56:15,294 --> 00:56:17,086
Also regarding the prayer of Janazah(جنازة),

809
00:56:18,106 --> 00:56:22,648
Imam Malik(إمام مالك), As-Shafie(ألشَّافعي) and Ahmed(أحمد) state that the prayer is not performed on the Shaheed(شَهِيد),

810
00:56:23,482 --> 00:56:25,954
but the scholars of Kufa(كوفه) and Basra(بسرى) state otherwise.

811
00:56:26,480 --> 00:56:29,845
The stronger opinion is that there is no prayer of Janazah(جنازة) for the Shaheed(شَهِيد).

812
00:56:30,834 --> 00:56:34,312
All of the above stated relates to the one, who dies on the battlefield.

813
00:56:34,352 --> 00:56:41,608
However, if a fighter is injured in the battlefield but then is rescued to another place, and is attended to.

814
00:56:42,264 --> 00:56:48,562
And then, eats and drinks, but eventually dies from his injuries, then such a person is washed

815
00:56:49,074 --> 00:56:50,572
and receives the prayer of Janazah(جنازة).

816
00:56:51,686 --> 00:56:56,230
This is what the Sahabah(صحابه) did, with Umar(عُمَر), when he was killed.

817
00:56:57,724 --> 00:56:59,729
We will close with this In Sha Allah(إنْ شاءالله),

818
00:57:00,357 --> 00:57:03,465
deal with the instruction and the virtues of the martyrs.

819
00:57:04,317 --> 00:57:05,043
Any questions?

820
00:57:05,570 --> 00:57:07,236
We still have any question from earlier.?

821
00:57:10,130 --> 00:57:20,172
In terms of the intention is done to free for example Muslim prisoners of war, or for ransom.

822
00:57:21,825 --> 00:57:25,962
That would be a valid intention because one would compare it to the Sarayah(سراية) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

823
00:57:26,051 --> 00:57:28,230
that he used to raid the caravans of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

824
00:57:30,619 --> 00:57:37,825
See if one would look at the general picture.

825
00:57:38,596 --> 00:57:43,550
Yes, it's true that they are causing some harm to the believers but it's all worldly harm.

826
00:57:46,713 --> 00:57:49,280
It's restricted to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

827
00:57:51,979 --> 00:57:58,772
The demolition of homes or killing some of the innocent people for example.

828
00:58:00,265 --> 00:58:06,390
So this is a worldly harm, but if one would look at the benefits of this,

829
00:58:07,781 --> 00:58:10,038
NUMBER ONE it's keeping the spirit Jihad(جهاد) alive.

830
00:58:12,390 --> 00:58:20,467
NUMBER TWO, it is keeping the enemy all the time, on the tip of their toes,

831
00:58:20,945 --> 00:58:24,729
they're always on guard, you're taking away from them their peace of mind,

832
00:58:25,505 --> 00:58:28,399
psychologically it is extremely detrimental on the enemy.

833
00:58:29,308 --> 00:58:30,655
The economy is suffering.

834
00:58:32,220 --> 00:58:35,744
And like one of Al-Mujahideen(مجاهدين) said:

835
00:58:37,545 --> 00:58:41,747
When your land is occupied, you do not have to win the battle against the occupier.

836
00:58:42,122 --> 00:58:44,055
All you have to do is keep the struggle going.

837
00:58:45,101 --> 00:58:47,862
In the end, the occupier will get tired pack up and leave.

838
00:58:49,192 --> 00:58:50,869
So you just keep on going.

839
00:58:51,119 --> 00:58:57,323
Obviously you will end up being harmed physically and more than the enemy.

840
00:58:58,387 --> 00:59:01,820
But the enemy eventually will get tired and will have to withdraw.

841
00:59:02,405 --> 00:59:07,585
So the thing is that the resistance needs to keep on going and should never go down, it's just carry on.

842
00:59:09,970 --> 00:59:12,956
إِن تَكونوا تَألَمونَ فَإِنَّهُم يَألَمونَ كَما تَألَمونَ ۖ

843
00:59:13,072 --> 00:59:15,919
If you're feeling pain, they are feeling pain just like you.

844
00:59:16,614 --> 00:59:18,216
وَتَرجونَ مِنَ اللَّهِ ما لا يَرجونَ ۗ

845
00:59:18,256 --> 00:59:20,478
And you are expecting from Allah, what they don't expect.

846
00:59:21,250 --> 00:59:23,298
So in the long term it's for the benefit of the Ummah(امة).

847
00:59:26,697 --> 00:59:33,088
Yani(يعني) I would see Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) is that it is inappropriate for him to actually die in the battlefield.

848
00:59:34,107 --> 00:59:35,716
 Why? Because he is the sword of Allah.

849
00:59:36,481 --> 00:59:39,693
So it's not befitting for the sword of Allah to be killed.

850
00:59:40,385 --> 00:59:47,721
Sword of Allah needs be, his soul needs to be taken away on his bed, safely.

851
00:59:49,711 --> 00:59:53,503
This Muslaha(مصلحة) and Mafsadah(مفسدة) thing was taken to the extreme

852
00:59:53,598 --> 01:00:00,699
and it's only limited to worldly calculations without getting the spiritual and Akhirah(آخرة) calculations in it.

853
01:00:01,183 --> 01:00:03,937
You know you always measure what's the Muslaha(مصلحة) and Mafsadah(مفسدة) in this

854
01:00:03,992 --> 01:00:08,263
and it's always looked at from a worldly point of view in terms of numbers and physical loss.

855
01:00:09,048 --> 01:00:12,217
If that's the case, then there's going to not going to be any battle.

856
01:00:12,749 --> 01:00:16,646
Because the assumption is that you want to win a war without any losses, that will never happened.

857
01:00:17,907 --> 01:00:20,848
Yani(يعني) Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) when he received the messenger from Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

858
01:00:20,927 --> 01:00:25,216
He said: What do you expect, you think that the Romans are going to walk out of their empire without a fight.

859
01:00:25,883 --> 01:00:28,895
هذا ما كنا نحن واِيَّكم ونعلم انه حاصل منهم

860
01:00:29,367 --> 01:00:30,821
We and you, already knew,

861
01:00:31,186 --> 01:00:34,954
ما كان قوم ليخرج من سلطانهم ويدع ملك هم بغير قتال

862
01:00:35,218 --> 01:00:38,796
People are not going to walk out of the kingdom and leave the reign without a fight.

863
01:00:39,708 --> 01:00:42,002
And then the dream that was seen by Sharhabil Bin Hasana(شرحبيل بن حسنة),

864
01:00:42,446 --> 01:00:45,784
رايتك انت والناس يمسكً وعد

865
01:00:46,216 --> 01:00:49,101
I saw you walking with the people on a very rough terrain.

866
01:00:49,391 --> 01:00:53,344
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: That is Jihad(جهاد) we suffer from it and our enemies suffer from it

867
01:00:53,701 --> 01:00:56,668
everybody suffers from it, suffering on both sides.

868
01:00:57,835 --> 01:01:04,238
However, on the side of the enemy, keep in mind that pharmacies in Israel(اسرائيل) are running out of depression medicine.

869
01:01:05,690 --> 01:01:08,117
So we need to always look at, all these calculations.

870
01:01:08,632 --> 01:01:15,919
I think it was two years ago, a 1 million people either stayed away from Israel(اسرائيل) or left Israel(اسرائيل).

871
01:01:16,697 --> 01:01:18,554
So it stopped immigration into the country.

872
01:01:19,332 --> 01:01:23,086
So there are some huge benefits that came out of this suicide bombings.

873
01:01:23,411 --> 01:01:31,605
And I think we mentioned before that that this will be the issue, this will be an issue of the future.

874
01:01:32,301 --> 01:01:34,542
Yani(يعني) where do you stand on the issue of suicide bombings

875
01:01:34,582 --> 01:01:41,657
because that is the one thing that no nuclear bombs, no deterrent force, no army, nothing can find the solution for it.

876
01:01:41,823 --> 01:01:45,369
 Somebody wants to die. What could you do to him? They want to die. You can't stop!

877
01:01:46,339 --> 01:01:51,186
The dearest thing to them, which is their life, they're willing to give it, you can't hold anything on them.

878
01:01:51,289 --> 01:01:52,448
You can twist their arms.

879
01:01:55,924 --> 01:01:59,876
Yani(يعني) Allah Alam(ألله أعلم)

880
01:02:00,130 --> 01:02:05,695
because and let's say that the Muslims are not even practicing and they're murdered, so that's the Shahadah(شَهَادَة)?

881
01:02:08,214 --> 01:02:12,202
So the intentions of the person in life their objectives life also have to play a role.

882
01:02:14,083 --> 01:02:24,201
Because there's a story I think we already read it, Al-Tartoshi(ألطرطوشي) mentions, about the man who asked to die without any pain.

883
01:02:25,368 --> 01:02:29,814
And he went to sleep in the garden and the enemy came and cut his head.

884
01:02:31,227 --> 01:02:34,516
So somebody saw him in a dream and told them, what happened to you?

885
01:02:34,556 --> 01:02:36,341
He said: I went to sleep and then just woke up in Jannah(جنة).

